{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3PyistcfZacTuV6ii2k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Browser suite: adopting an input whose `value` attribute differs from the bound value sets the property to the bound value.\n[x] Browser suite: after adoption, the user-edit-survives and bound-value-wins pair from ticket 06 holds for the adopted input.\n[x] Browser suite: adopting a checked checkbox whose bound value is `true` produces no write; a bound `false` unchecks it.\n\nTicket 07 is done and committed in two commits. Final checks pass: `npm test` (424 passing), `npm run test:ssr` (112 passing) and lint.\n\n**Where I departed from the wording:** the ticket says the first comparison on adopt is \"against the live DOM property\". If I did that literally, a value typed before hydration would be overwritten, which the first checklist item forbids. So the first comparison is against what the server wrote: `defaultValue`, `defaultChecked` or `defaultSelected`, which come from the HTML attributes. A `select` has none of these, so it falls back to the live property. Later runs compare against the per-element record from ticket 06.\n\n**A second bug the region test caught:** on adopt, `_bindEl` skips static attribute values. That meant a control's static `value` never got into the record, so the next run of the region wrote it again and overwrote the visitor's edit. Now an adopted control's static value goes through the same keep-if-matching check, via a new `_ctl` helper that `_setAttr` also uses. All other static attributes are still left untouched on adopt.\n\n**Tests:** five new `adopt:` tests in `test/index.ts`. Three of them fail on the source before this ticket: the typed value surviving adoption, the edit surviving a region re-run, and the checkbox the visitor unchecked before hydration. The other two (a differing attribute gets written, a bound `false` unchecks) also pass on the old code; I kept them as regression guards.\n\n**Size:** the browser templater went from 4.94 kB to 4.98 kB, 28 B over its 4.95 kB limit. Following the spec's rounding rule, I raised the limit to 5 kB and recorded why in `.size-limit.js`.\n\nI also added a paragraph to AGENTS.md on how adopted controls are compared. My notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":234,"cache_read_input_tokens":74221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":234},"output_tokens":684,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2f196ac-3997-4753-a2a5-e49656ab8a81","uuid":"1ead13eb-40ca-4996-96b6-047b259ada82","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:32:30.669Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3Pyic1dKYJ8MS2TnEWC"}
